## Scope notes (not blockers)
- `Model.base` has a dataclass default (`""`) placed last: `tests/test_fetch.py` and `tests/test_server.py` construct `Model(...)` directly and are outside the permitted file set. `load()` still requires `base` on every row; five new tests pin it.
- The shell's literal `cmp` in `osaurus_restore_check` is now the module's `filecmp.cmp(shallow=False)`, because `restore` removes the backup on success, so a shell `cmp` afterwards would have nothing to compare and would be a second definition. The printed verdict and trap behaviour are unchanged. A scratch-`HOME` run of `osaurus_pin` → `osaurus_restore_check` pinned (900/false/false), logged one JSON line each, restored both files byte-identical (`cmp`), removed the backup, and left `config/osaurus-settings-baseline.json` clean.
- The dry check caught a real defect: `config_dir`/`baseline_path` arriving as strings (the shell interpolates them into `python -c`) broke `write_baseline`; coerced with `Path(...)` and pinned by `test_pin_and_restore_accept_the_strings_the_shell_hands_them`.
- Not verified: no server, runtime, model or canary was run; no measured run; `~/.osaurus` was never read or written (the round-trip used a scratch `HOME`).
